{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey security deposit cap and annual increase limit","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit of more than one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly increase in the security deposit may not exceed 10% of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in New Jersey where the landlord chooses to collect a security deposit; collecting a deposit is optional but the prescribed rules then apply.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and double-damages remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy terminates, a landlord must return the security deposit plus interest less lawful deductions, and must send an itemized list of any deductions by registered or certified mail within the same 30 days.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in New Jersey; where a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation the deposit is due within five business days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"If the deposit is not returned within 30 days, the court may award the tenant double the amount wrongly withheld plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Interest on security deposits belongs to the tenant","requirement":"Interest or earnings paid on a security deposit belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited toward rent on the lease renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 where the tenant received written notice of that payment date.","key_value":"paid on lease renewal or anniversary, or January 31","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental units in New Jersey where a security deposit is held.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19(c)","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the renewal or anniversary of the tenant’s lease or on January 31, if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year (N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 (c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit account notice and tenant self-help remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days of receiving a security deposit, and at each annual interest payment, a landlord must tell the tenant in writing the name and address of the bank or investment company, the amount deposited, the account type and the current interest rate.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential landlords holding security deposit money in New Jersey; account type rules differ for landlords of ten or fewer units and ten or more units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"notice duty applies to any landlord holding a deposit"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A tenant who does not receive proper notice or interest may apply the deposit plus interest at 7% per annum to rent after written notice to the landlord; the landlord then may not demand an additional deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1(c)","quoted_span":"Within 30 days of receipt of the security deposit and at the time of each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the name and address of the banking institution or investment company in which the money is deposited, the amount of the deposit, type of account, and current rate of interest for the account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and notify the tenant in writing within three business days of when and where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a residential lease early under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"This law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
